# lint-staged runs per workspace package; add a line here when an app joins.
#
# Every app is now covered (#138 closed the tb-addon gap). What is NOT covered is
# packages/pg-js and examples/*: they declare no prettier config, so a line here
# would format them against prettier's bare defaults rather than a style anyone
# chose. Give a package a config first, then add its line — and note that a
# config at the REPO ROOT is not the way to do it, because prettier resolves
# config by walking up from each file and a package.json without a `prettier` key
# does not stop the search, so one root config silently becomes the style of
# every package that has none. See apps/tb-addon/CLAUDE.md.
#
# Each line runs with that package's directory as cwd, which is what makes the
# package's own prettier config and .prettierignore apply.
pnpm --filter postguard-website exec lint-staged
pnpm --filter postguard-outlook-addin exec lint-staged
pnpm --filter postguard-tb-addon exec lint-staged
